# Paired Route: Mining + Engineering 1-300 (WoW: Forever)
# Follows docs/MULTI_PROFESSION_RULES.md:
# - Dedicated per-combination file: guides/pairs/mining-engineering.guide
# - Single-anchor sections on Engineering (crafting anchor) in rising order,
#   so Polestar's section auto-skip and remaining-material subtraction work
#   cleanly; Mining trainers, skill checkpoints and ore loops are
#   interleaved inside each Engineering bracket.
# - Every `collect ... gather Mining <rank>` keeps its matching `auction`
#   goal in the same section (carried over from guides/engineering.guide),
#   so Mix / Gather / Buy modes all work.
# - Engineering crafts, kept intermediates and spell ids follow
#   guides/engineering.guide; Mining trainers, node loops and rank gates
#   follow guides/mining.guide. Both were resolved from the Forever client
#   tables (build 1.60.1).
# - Forever scarce material: Bauxite (bonus drop from Gold Veins, Mithril
#   Deposits and Indurium veins) feeds Sandpaper, an Engineering recipe
#   that unlocks at 130 (2 Bauxite + 1 Bolt of Linen Cloth; ids resolved
#   with `polestar find`: Bauxite 249425, Sandpaper 249432, spell 1249634,
#   Bolt of Linen Cloth 2996). Sandpaper goes into 25 Blacksmithing
#   recipes, so it sells well and is worth hoarding Bauxite for.
# - Forever camp feature: the Engineering Reagent Bot (recipe from skill 20,
#   item 279950) sits on a Basic Campfire as one of its three features.
# - Tips are original prose for this pack.

guide forever-professions/pair-mining-engineering
title Mining + Engineering 1-300
category Professions
folder Paired Routes
coords era
levels 1-60
zone Azeroth
keywords mining, engineering, paired, bauxite, sandpaper

pitch Level Mining and Engineering together from 1 to 300: your own picks supply the stone and bars every bomb, tube and widget eats.
pro Mine the Rough, Coarse, Heavy, Solid and Dense Stone and every bar the Engineering route needs, so most of it costs nothing
pro Scarce Bauxite from Gold, Mithril and Indurium nodes turns into Sandpaper (Engineering 130), a high-demand Blacksmithing input, and the Reagent Bot camp feature is yours
con Uses both primary slots and Engineering is bar-hungry, so Mining sometimes lags behind the crafting bands; top up from the Auction House when it does

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Apprentice

section Engineering 1-75

step Learn Engineering
  only Alliance
  zone Ironforge
  tip Engineering takes a primary slot and Mining takes the other one. Jemma Quikswitch in Ironforge teaches Apprentice Engineering at any character level. Buy a Blacksmith Hammer now: most recipes need one in your bags. From Engineering 20 you can also learn Reagent Bot, an Engineering camp feature: a Basic Campfire (Cooking 1) hosts up to three features, and this is one of them.
  train Engineering Apprentice npc 11028

step Learn Engineering
  only Horde
  zone Orgrimmar
  tip Engineering takes a primary slot and Mining takes the other one. Thund in Orgrimmar teaches Apprentice Engineering at any character level. Buy a Blacksmith Hammer now: most recipes need one in your bags. From Engineering 20 you can also learn Reagent Bot, an Engineering camp feature: a Basic Campfire (Cooking 1) hosts up to three features, and this is one of them.
  train Engineering Apprentice npc 2857

step Learn Mining
  only Alliance
  zone Elwynn Forest
  tip Kelsey Fargo in Elwynn Forest teaches Apprentice Mining at any character level. Buy a Mining Pick: keep it in your bags, it does not need to be equipped but you cannot mine without it. Switch on Find Minerals in the Mining box of the Professions window and drag it onto your bar; it turns itself off when you die, and you can only track minerals or herbs, not both.
  train Mining Apprentice npc 247226
  buy 2901 x1 nearest

step Learn Mining
  only Horde
  zone Durotar
  tip Norzsh in the Valley of Trials teaches Apprentice Mining at any character level. Buy a Mining Pick: keep it in your bags, it does not need to be equipped but you cannot mine without it. Switch on Find Minerals in the Mining box of the Professions window and drag it onto your bar; it turns itself off when you die, and you can only track minerals or herbs, not both.
  train Mining Apprentice npc 267328
  buy 2901 x1 nearest

step Copper in Elwynn Forest
  only Alliance
  zone Elwynn Forest
  tip Mine every Copper Vein and Poor Copper Vein on the loop until Mining 65. Poor Copper Veins give Copper Ore and Rough Stone from skill 1, which is exactly what the first Engineering crafts use, so save every Rough Stone and smelt the ore at the Goldshire forge. The cave veins regrow quickly; sweep them first if your level allows.
  goto 47.3,32.3 "Poor Copper Vein" r 30
  goto 52.1,32.4 "Poor Copper Vein" r 30
  goto 56.2,37.9 "Poor Copper Vein" r 30
  goto 57.3,50.4 "Poor Copper Vein" r 30
  goto 48.9,48.8 "Poor Copper Vein" r 30
  goto 30.2,54.0 "Copper Vein" r 30
  goto 28.1,66.2 "Copper Vein" r 30
  skill Mining 65

step Copper in Durotar
  only Horde
  zone Durotar
  tip Mine every Copper Vein and Poor Copper Vein on the loop until Mining 65. Poor Copper Veins give Copper Ore and Rough Stone from skill 1, which is exactly what the first Engineering crafts use, so save every Rough Stone and smelt the ore at the Razor Hill forge. Mulgore's cave is a quieter alternative.
  goto 42.1,68.1 "Poor Copper Vein" r 30
  goto 45.4,72.8 "Poor Copper Vein" r 30
  goto 46.7,62.4 "Poor Copper Vein" r 30
  goto 42.5,58.1 "Poor Copper Vein" r 30
  goto 43.3,53.4 "Poor Copper Vein" r 30
  goto 36.0,45.4 "Copper Vein" r 30
  goto 35.6,35.5 "Copper Vein" r 30
  skill Mining 65

step Engineering 1-75: Auction House
  tip What the first bombs take that the Auction House sells: 52 Rough Stone, 58 Copper Bar, 26 Linen Cloth. The counts drop by what your bags, bank and mail hold.
  auction 2835 x52
  auction 2840 x58
  auction 2589 x26

step Engineering 1-75: stone, bars and cloth
  tip Rough Stone comes from Copper Veins while mining; Copper Bar is smelted from Copper Ore; Linen Cloth drops from humanoids of level 5-20. Gather them while you level, or take them from your bank.
  collect 2835 x52 anywhere gather Mining 1
  collect 2840 x58 anywhere gather Mining 1
  collect 2589 x26 anywhere gather levels 5-20

step Engineering 1-75: tools
  tip A Blacksmith Hammer from any Blacksmithing or Engineering supply vendor, usually next to the trainer. Keep it in your bags: most recipes need it.
  buy 5956 x1 nearest

step Rough Blasting Powder, Copper Bolts, Arclight Spanner, Rough Copper Bomb (1-75)
  tip Rough Blasting Powder, 52 crafts to 35: one Rough Stone each. Keep all of it. Then Handful of Copper Bolts, 26 crafts to 55: one Copper Bar each. Keep all of those too. Then one Arclight Spanner: six Copper Bars, and keep it, you need it to craft Engineering recipes. Then Rough Copper Bomb, 26 crafts to 75: a Copper Bar, a bolt, two powders and a Linen Cloth each. It turns yellow at 60, so make a few more if you come up short, and do not craft them all at once unless Journeyman is already learned: the bombs may carry you past 75.
  learn 3918 "Rough Blasting Powder"
  craft 3918 "Rough Blasting Powder" until 35
  learn 3922 "Handful of Copper Bolts"
  craft 3922 "Handful of Copper Bolts" until 55
  learn 7430 "Arclight Spanner"
  craft 7430 "Arclight Spanner" x1
  learn 3923 "Rough Copper Bomb"
  craft 3923 "Rough Copper Bomb" until 75

