step Tin and Silver in the Wetlands
  only Alliance
  zone Wetlands
  tip Tin Veins need Mining 65 and Silver Veins 75. The Wetlands cave is full of Tin Veins and Incendicite with a very fast regrow; its mobs are around level 20, so outlevel them by a few levels. Coarse Stone (for the Coarse Blasting Powder) comes off Tin Veins, so keep all of it, and smelt leftover Copper and Tin into Bronze: Bronze stops giving skill around 105.
  goto 47.5,62.1 "Incendicite Mineral Vein, Tin Vein" r 30
  goto 51.2,61.6 "Incendicite Mineral Vein, Tin Vein" r 30
  goto 24.0,60.0 "Copper Vein, Tin Vein" r 30
  goto 25.8,50.2 "Copper Vein, Tin Vein" r 30
  goto 27.8,38.0 "Copper Vein, Tin Vein" r 30
  skill Mining 105

step Tin and Silver in Hillsbrad Foothills
  only Horde
  zone Hillsbrad Foothills
  tip Tin Veins need Mining 65 and Silver Veins 75. Hillsbrad Foothills is the best open route for this band; expect company, and smelt at Tarren Mill. Coarse Stone (for the Coarse Blasting Powder) comes off Tin Veins, so keep all of it, and smelt leftover Copper and Tin into Bronze: Bronze stops giving skill around 105.
  goto 31.5,57.5 "Tin Vein, Silver Vein" r 30
  goto 27.6,57.5 "Tin Vein, Silver Vein" r 30
  goto 31.4,52.7 "Tin Vein, Silver Vein" r 30
  goto 40.7,53.4 "Copper Vein, Tin Vein" r 30
  goto 38.5,63.8 "Copper Vein, Tin Vein" r 30
  skill Mining 105

step Engineering 75-105: Auction House
  tip What the next explosives take that the Auction House sells: 51 Coarse Stone, 17 Linen Cloth, 5 Silver Bar. The counts drop by what your bags, bank and mail hold.
  auction 2836 x51
  auction 2589 x17
  auction 2842 x5

step Engineering 75-105: stone, cloth and bars
  tip Coarse Stone comes from Tin Veins while mining; Linen Cloth drops from humanoids of level 5-20; Silver Bar is smelted from Silver Ore (Mining 75). Gather them while you level, or take them from your bank.
  collect 2836 x51 anywhere gather Mining 65
  collect 2589 x17 anywhere gather levels 5-20
  collect 2842 x5 anywhere gather Mining 75

step Coarse Blasting Powder, Coarse Dynamite, Silver Contact (75-105)
  tip Coarse Blasting Powder, 51 crafts to 90: one Coarse Stone each. Keep all of it. Then Coarse Dynamite, 17 crafts to 100: three powders and a Linen Cloth each. It turns green at 97, so start the Silver Contacts if you come up short. Then Silver Contact, 5 crafts to 105: a Silver Bar each, five contacts a craft. If Silver Bar is expensive, make Flying Tiger Goggles instead (30 Light Leather, 10 Tigerseye).
  learn 3929 "Coarse Blasting Powder"
  craft 3929 "Coarse Blasting Powder" until 90
  learn 3931 "Coarse Dynamite"
  craft 3931 "Coarse Dynamite" until 100
  learn 3973 "Silver Contact"
  craft 3973 "Silver Contact" until 105

