  auction 2592 x30

step Engineering 160-175: cloth
  tip Wool Cloth drops from humanoids of level 15-30. Gather it while you level, or take it from your bank.
  collect 2592 x30 anywhere gather levels 15-30

step Explosive Sheep (160-175)
  tip Explosive Sheep, 15 crafts to 175: two kept Heavy Blasting Powders, a kept Whirring Bronze Gizmo, a kept Bronze Framework and two Wool Cloths each. Keep 5 of the sheep: they may be needed for Goblin Engineering at 200.
  learn 3955 "Explosive Sheep"
  craft 3955 "Explosive Sheep" until 175

section Engineering 175-200

step Mithril in the Hinterlands
  zone The Hinterlands
  tip Mithril Deposits need Mining 175 and Truesilver Deposits 230. Mine toward Mining 200 here: the 120 Solid Stone, 18 Mithril Bars and the Steel Bars all come off this loop, and Mithril is a good Bauxite source. Skip the red-marked route where level 62 elites patrol. Tanaris is the alternative for level 60s.
  goto 20.8,58.8 "Mithril Deposit, Truesilver Deposit" r 30
  goto 25.1,68.8 "Mithril Deposit, Truesilver Deposit" r 30
  goto 33.3,60.6 "Mithril Deposit, Truesilver Deposit" r 30
  goto 41.0,66.1 "Mithril Deposit, Truesilver Deposit" r 30
  goto 35.5,74.8 "Mithril Deposit, Truesilver Deposit" r 30
  goto 50.1,71.6 "Mithril Deposit, Truesilver Deposit" r 30
  skill Mining 200

step Engineering 175-200: Auction House
  tip What the next parts take that the Auction House sells: 120 Solid Stone, 4 Steel Bar, 18 Mithril Bar. The counts drop by what your bags, bank and mail hold.
  auction 7912 x120
  auction 3859 x4
  auction 3860 x18

step Engineering 175-200: stone and bars
  tip Solid Stone comes from Mithril Deposits while mining; Steel Bar is smelted from an Iron Bar and a Coal (Mining 165); Mithril Bar is smelted from Mithril Ore (Mining 175). Gather them while you level, or take them from your bank.
  collect 7912 x120 anywhere gather Mining 175
  collect 3859 x4 anywhere gather Mining 165
  collect 3860 x18 anywhere gather Mining 175

step Solid Blasting Powder, Gyromatic Micro-Adjustor, Mithril Tube (175-200)
  tip Solid Blasting Powder, 60 crafts to 194: two Solid Stone each. Keep all of it: the triggers and the bombs need it later. Then one Gyromatic Micro-Adjustor: four Steel Bars, and keep it, some Engineering recipes need it to craft. Then Mithril Tube, 6 crafts to 200: three Mithril Bars each. Keep all six: they may be needed for Gnomish Engineering at 200. If the Adjustor does not land the point to 195, craft a few Iron Grenades or any other recipe that still gives skill points. At 200 and level 30 you can pick a specialization, Gnomish or Goblin: optional, not needed to level.
  learn 12585 "Solid Blasting Powder"
  craft 12585 "Solid Blasting Powder" until 194
  learn 12590 "Gyromatic Micro-Adjustor"
  craft 12590 "Gyromatic Micro-Adjustor" x1
  learn 12589 "Mithril Tube"
  craft 12589 "Mithril Tube" until 200

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Artisan

section Engineering 200-238

step Artisan Engineering
  zone Tanaris
  tip Artisan Engineering raises the cap to 300; it needs skill 200 and character level 35. Buzzek Bracketswing in Gadgetzan, Tanaris, teaches both factions, right outside the inn near the mailbox. He also teaches the recipes above 200, so come as soon as you reach 200.
  level 35
  train Engineering Artisan npc 8736

step Artisan Mining
  only Alliance
  zone Ironforge
  tip Artisan Mining raises the cap to 300, needs skill 200 and costs 5 gold. Geofram Bouldertoe in Ironforge teaches it; sort it out before the Mithril farm, because Mining stalls at 225 otherwise.
  train Mining Artisan npc 4254

step Artisan Mining
  only Horde
  zone Orgrimmar
  tip Artisan Mining raises the cap to 300, needs skill 200 and costs 5 gold. Makaru in Orgrimmar teaches it; sort it out before the Mithril farm, because Mining stalls at 225 otherwise.
  train Mining Artisan npc 3357

step Mithril and Truesilver in the Hinterlands
  zone The Hinterlands
  tip Run the same Hinterlands loop up to Mining 245; Truesilver Deposits open at 230. The 140 Mithril Bars for the casings come off this ground, and Mithril Deposits keep dropping Bauxite for later Sandpaper.
