step Hi-Explosive Bomb, Dense Blasting Powder (238-260)
  tip Hi-Explosive Bomb, 20 crafts to 250: two kept Mithril Casings, a kept Unstable Trigger and two kept Solid Blasting Powders each, four bombs a craft. Then Dense Blasting Powder, 44 crafts to 260: two Dense Stone each. Keep the powder: the Thorium Grenades of the PvP variant need it.
  learn 12619 "Hi-Explosive Bomb"
  craft 12619 "Hi-Explosive Bomb" until 250
  learn 19788 "Dense Blasting Powder"
  craft 19788 "Dense Blasting Powder" until 260

section Engineering 260-280

step Schematic: Thorium Widget
  tip The schematic is sold by Sovik in Orgrimmar and Gearcutter Cogspinner in Ironforge, limited stock.
  buy 16042 x1 nearest

step Rich Thorium in Un'Goro Crater
  zone Un'Goro Crater
  tip Rich Thorium Veins open at Mining 275, and you want 186 Thorium Bars across the last two Engineering brackets, so settle into this loop. The veins cluster in the west and south of the crater. Winterspring is the alternative: mostly manageable caves, but the gorge has patrolling elites. Skip Eastern Plaguelands unless you are geared or stealthed.
  goto 23.4,61.0 "Small Thorium Vein, Rich Thorium Vein" r 30
  goto 24.7,49.8 "Small Thorium Vein" r 30
  goto 52.7,47.3 "Rich Thorium Vein" r 30
  goto 45.5,64.8 "Small Thorium Vein" r 30
  goto 50.5,75.6 "Small Thorium Vein" r 30
  goto 59.5,65.4 "Small Thorium Vein" r 30
  skill Mining 300

step Engineering 260-280: Auction House
  tip What the widgets take that the Auction House sells: 60 Thorium Bar, 20 Runecloth. The counts drop by what your bags, bank and mail hold.
  auction 12359 x60
  auction 14047 x20

step Engineering 260-280: bars and cloth
  tip Thorium Bar is smelted from Thorium Ore (Mining 250); Runecloth drops from humanoids of level 45-60. Gather them while you level, or take them from your bank.
  collect 12359 x60 anywhere gather Mining 250
  collect 14047 x20 anywhere gather levels 45-60

step Thorium Widget (260-280)
  tip Thorium Widget, 20 crafts to 280: three Thorium Bars and a Runecloth each. Use the schematic first to learn it. PvP variant: make only 10 widgets (30 Thorium Bar, 10 Runecloth), then 10 Thorium Grenades (a widget, 3 Thorium Bars, 3 Dense Blasting Powders and 3 Runecloth each; Schematic: Thorium Grenade from the same two vendors). If the grenades sell well, keep making widgets and grenades to 290 (about 8 of each, needs 10 more Dense Blasting Powder), then only 12 Thorium Tubes are needed.
  learn 19791 "Thorium Widget"
  craft 19791 "Thorium Widget" until 280

section Engineering 280-300

step Schematic: Thorium Tube
  tip The schematic is sold by Xizzer Fizzbolt in Everlook, Winterspring, first building on the right after the gate. It binds when picked up in Forever: buy it with the character leveling Engineering.
  buy 16047 x1 nearest

step Engineering 280-300: Auction House
  tip What the tubes take that the Auction House sells: 126 Thorium Bar. The counts drop by what your bags, bank and mail hold.
  auction 12359 x126

step Engineering 280-300: bars
  tip Thorium Bar is smelted from Thorium Ore (Mining 250). Smelt your own ore, or take the bars from your bank.
  collect 12359 x126 anywhere gather Mining 250

step Thorium Tube (280-300)
  tip Thorium Tube, 21 crafts to 300: six Thorium Bars each. It turns yellow at 295, so make a few more if you come up short of 300. Use the schematic first to learn it. If you hold world-drop Schematic: Thorium Shells, make 5 tubes to 285, then 15 Thorium Shells (30 Thorium Bar, 15 Dense Blasting Powder; one craft makes 200 shells). With Mining at 300 as well, Pitchblende from Thorium veins is saved for Azerothium Bars, and any spare Sandpaper can go to your Blacksmith.
  learn 19795 "Thorium Tube"
  craft 19795 "Thorium Tube" until 300
